WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.266
These readings look at attempts to restrain fast moving technologies.

00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:09.234
Scientists paused their own work on recombinant DNA.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.516
The government tried to control encryption.

00:00:12.516 --> 00:00:15.951
And in 2023, a letter asked AI labs to pause.

00:00:15.951 --> 00:00:19.920
The question is who decides, and who is in the room.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:25.682
The CRISPR Democracy essay says Asilomar was a poor model for governing new gene

00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:26.691
editing tools.

00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:29.860
The scientists were skilled and responsible.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.606
But the meeting was narrow, with few outside voices,

00:00:33.606 --> 00:00:36.560
and it framed risk only as lab accidents.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.875
In 1993 the White House announced the Clipper Chip.

00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:45.270
It was a voluntary program, presented as a way to protect privacy while meeting the

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.895
needs of law enforcement.

00:00:46.895 --> 00:00:49.950
The statement claimed the chip would be strong,

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.240
and more secure than many voice encryption systems then available.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.207
Clipper relied on key escrow.

00:00:56.207 --> 00:01:00.210
Each device had keys that were split and stored separately.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.145
Officials could obtain them only with legal authorization.

00:01:04.145 --> 00:01:07.605
The government argued this was a balanced approach.

00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:10.726
Critics saw a back door built into encryption,

00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:13.440
which is the debate that kept returning.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.361
The Future of Life Institute letter calls for a pause on training AI systems more

00:01:19.361 --> 00:01:20.823
powerful than GPT-4.

00:01:20.823 --> 00:01:24.332
It asks that the pause be public and verifiable.

00:01:24.332 --> 00:01:30.400
If labs will not act quickly, it says governments should step in with a moratorium.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.092
The takeaway is to ask where the choice was, and who made it.

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:37.400
Asilomar left many people out.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.092
Clipper was designed by government.

00:01:40.092 --> 00:01:45.169
The AI letter says big decisions must not be left to tech leaders.

00:01:45.169 --> 00:01:48.400
Ask whether these precedents truly fit AI.
